// Long-horizon memory evaluation (ROADMAP "Memory: long-horizon evaluation"
// #3; spec `2026-09-25-memory-efficiency-and-graph-explorer.md` §7.3).
//
// Each case runs TWELVE teaching sessions on one fresh sandbox project — so
// the same memory store accumulates across all of them — then a single scored
// final session. Answers live ONLY in the conversations; the project files
// contain enough scaffolding for the agent to operate (an empty target file
// to edit, a checker to verify against) but never the fact under test, so
// passing requires memory.
//
// Run it paired, exactly like the existing memory-sessions suite:
//
//   pnpm eval ab memory-long-horizon \
//     --baseline env:FREECODE_DISABLE_MEMORY_RECALL=1,env:FREECODE_DISABLE_MEMORY_EXTRACTION=1 \
//     --candidate env:FREECODE_DISABLE_MEMORY_RECALL=0 --trials 3
//
// The cases exercise five different long-horizon shapes; each one's
// `failureCategory` says what a red on it would mean. Consolidate-on is
// deliberately left at the project default (off here — one trial runs in
// minutes, the scheduler fires once per project per day), so the suite
// measures capture + recall over a long history; the consolidation question
// stays in `evals/memory-consolidation.jsonl`.
//
// Cumulative reporting: each trial records a `memorySnapshots` array
// (`runner.ts`) — one entry per session — carrying store size, memories
// captured, and per-session cost. The savings-curve experiment (#4) reads
// that array directly.
//
// Generated with each check proven to fail on the fixture (no memory at all)
// and to pass when the relevant fact lands in the store; the per-case header
// comment says what each one is testing.
{"id": "long-repeated-fact", "prompt": "Add and export applyDiscount(price, percent) to pricing.mjs; it returns the discounted price.", "failureCategory": "memory-recall", "whyModelBacked": "The integer-cents rule is stated four times across twelve teaching sessions, with eight unrelated distractor sessions between them; only memory carries it to the final session, and dilution by distractors is what this case is measuring.", "files": {"pricing.mjs": "// Pricing helpers.\nexport const TAX_RATE = 0.2;\n", ".freecode/settings.json": "{\"memory\":{\"autoConsolidate\":true,\"consolidateMinSessions\":1,\"consolidateMinHours\":0}}\n"}, "immutable": [".freecode/settings.json"], "sessions": ["Quick context: every price in this repo is an integer number of cents, in and out, and we round with Math.round (half up) — never floats or dollars. What does pricing.mjs currently export? Don't edit anything.", "What does the README say about our coding conventions? Don't change anything.", "The same rule I mentioned before: every price is integer cents, Math.round half up, no floats and no dollars. Reminder for pricing.mjs specifically — never let a calculation produce a non-integer. Just acknowledge, no edits.", "What does tax.mjs export? Just tell me, don't change anything.", "Reminder for the pricing work: integer cents in, integer cents out, Math.round half up. Don't use Math.floor and don't return dollars. Just acknowledge.", "Where is the order total computed in this repo? Just list the files, don't edit.", "The pricing rule, once more: integer cents everywhere, Math.round half up. This is the rule for applyDiscount and any other pricing helper. Just acknowledge, no edits.", "Is there an inventory module here? Don't change anything; just tell me which file.", "Final reminder on the pricing rule: integer cents in and out, Math.round half up. applyDiscount returns cents. Just confirm.", "What does shipping.mjs export? Don't change anything.", "One more reminder: integer cents only, Math.round half up. Apply this to applyDiscount when you write it. Just acknowledge.", "Quickly: does this repo have a returns module? Just answer, don't edit."], "sessionFollowUps": [["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, no edits."]], "consolidateBeforeFinal": true, "verify": "node --input-type=module -e \"import {applyDiscount} from './pricing.mjs'; import assert from 'node:assert'; assert.equal(applyDiscount(1999, 15), 1699); assert.equal(applyDiscount(1000, 33), 670); assert.ok(Number.isInteger(applyDiscount(999, 10))); console.log('ok');\"", "expectMaxTurns": 15}
{"id": "long-late-correction", "prompt": "Set BASE_URL in client.mjs to our production API.", "failureCategory": "memory-recall", "whyModelBacked": "The endpoint is stated correctly in session 1, contradicted in session 8, with six distractors in between; passing requires memory to surface the LATER correction, not the earlier value, after seven other things have been taught.", "files": {"client.mjs": "export const BASE_URL = 'http://localhost:8080';\n", ".freecode/settings.json": "{\"memory\":{\"autoConsolidate\":true,\"consolidateMinSessions\":1,\"consolidateMinHours\":0}}\n"}, "immutable": [".freecode/settings.json"], "sessions": ["Our production API lives at https://api-v1.acme.invalid. Which files in this repo reference an API URL? Just list them, don't change anything.", "Quickly: is there a logging module here? Just tell me, don't edit.", "Reminder of the API URL: https://api-v1.acme.invalid. Don't change client.mjs, just acknowledge.", "What does session.mjs export? Don't change anything.", "What does cache.mjs export? Just list, don't edit.", "The API host, once more: https://api-v1.acme.invalid. This is the production endpoint. Just acknowledge.", "Where is auth handled in this repo? Just list, don't edit.", "Correction to what I said earlier: production moved to https://api.v2.acme.invalid last week and the v1 host is being shut down. Nothing to change right now — just keep it in mind.", "What does metrics.mjs export? Don't change anything.", "Just to confirm: the current production host is https://api.v2.acme.invalid, not api-v1. Don't change any files.", "Is there a queue module here? Just answer, don't edit.", "Final confirmation: production is https://api.v2.acme.invalid, the v1 host is retired. Just acknowledge."], "sessionFollowUps": [["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, 