{"id": "long-gap-survival", "prompt": "Add and export formatDate(date) in dates.mjs that formats a Date for the invoice footer.", "failureCategory": "memory-recall", "whyModelBacked": "The date convention is taught in sessions 1–3, then nine unrelated sessions pass before the probe; tests whether a memory still surfaces after the store has been filled with later chatter of equal surface relevance.", "files": {"dates.mjs": "// Date helpers for invoices.\n", "invoice.mjs": "import { formatDate } from './dates.mjs';\nexport const footer = (d) => `Issued ${formatDate(d)}`;\n", ".freecode/settings.json": "{\"memory\":{\"autoConsolidate\":true,\"consolidateMinSessions\":1,\"consolidateMinHours\":0}}\n"}, "immutable": [".freecode/settings.json"], "sessions": ["Quick question before next week's invoice work: our rule here is that every user-facing date is ISO 8601 YYYY-MM-DD in UTC — locale formats once caused a billing dispute between our US and German clients. Does anything in invoice.mjs look like it formats dates? Just answer, don't change files.", "What does tax.mjs export? Don't change anything.", "Reminder: dates in this repo are ISO 8601 YYYY-MM-DD in UTC, for the same billing reason. Don't change files, just acknowledge.", "Quickly: is there a shipping module? Just answer, don't edit.", "What does currency.mjs export? Just list, don't change anything.", "The dates rule, once more: ISO 8601 YYYY-MM-DD in UTC for every user-facing date. Just acknowledge.", "Where is the total computed in this repo? Just list, don't edit.", "What does discount.mjs export? Just answer, don't change anything.", "Quickly: does this repo have a returns module? Just answer, don't edit.", "What does inventory.mjs export? Just list, don't change anything.", "What does session.mjs export? Just answer, don't change anything.", "Is there a queue module here? Just answer, don't edit."], "sessionFollowUps": [["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, no edits."]], "consolidateBeforeFinal": true, "verify": "node --input-type=module -e \"import {formatDate} from './dates.mjs'; import assert from 'node:assert'; assert.equal(formatDate(new Date(Date.UTC(2026,0,5,23,30))), '2026-01-05'); assert.equal(formatDate(new Date(Date.UTC(2025,11,31))), '2025-12-31'); console.log('ok');\"", "expectMaxTurns": 15}
{"id": "long-incremental-assembly", "prompt": "Implement and export taxCents(amount, region) in tax.mjs that returns the tax in integer cents. The repo rule is every monetary value is integer cents; use Math.round half up. Tax rates are configured per region.", "failureCategory": "memory-recall", "whyModelBacked": "Three distinct facts are needed: integer-cents-only, Math.round-half-up rounding, and the per-region tax rate map. They are split across six teaching sessions (two facts per session); the probe asks for code that needs ALL of them at once. Tests whether fragmented teaching still produces a complete memory.", "files": {"tax.mjs": "// Tax helpers.\nexport const REGION = 'us-east-1';\n", "regions.mjs": "// Region table.\nexport const RATES = {};\n", ".freecode/settings.json": "{\"memory\":{\"autoConsolidate\":true,\"consolidateMinSessions\":1,\"consolidateMinHours\":0}}\n"}, "immutable": ["regions.mjs", ".freecode/settings.json"], "sessions": ["Quick context for the tax work: every monetary value in this repo is integer cents in and out, and we round with Math.round (half up) — never floats and never dollars. Just acknowledge, no edits.", "The region's tax rate for us-east-1 is 8.875 percent. That's a number, not a string. Don't change files, just acknowledge.", "Quickly: what does tax.mjs currently export? Just tell me, don't change anything.", "For eu-west-2 the tax rate is 20 percent. The rate table lives in regions.mjs. Don't change files yet, just acknowledge.", "Reminder of the cents rule: integer cents in and out, Math.round half up. Apply this to any tax helper. Just acknowledge, no edits.", "The region table also needs ap-northeast-1 at 10 percent. Don't change files, just acknowledge."], "sessionFollowUps": [["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, no edits."]], "consolidateBeforeFinal": true, "verify": "node --input-type=module -e \"import {taxCents} from './tax.mjs'; import assert from 'node:assert'; assert.equal(taxCents(10000, 'us-east-1'), 888); assert.equal(taxCents(10000, 'eu-west-2'), 2000); assert.equal(taxCents(10000, 'ap-northeast-1'), 1000); assert.equal(taxCents(1999, 'us-east-1'), Math.round(1999*0.08875)); console.log('ok');\"", "expectMaxTurns": 15}
{"id": "long-irrelevant-chatter-control", "prompt": "sum() in math.mjs returns the wrong result. Fix it.", "failureCategory": "memory-recall", "whyModelBacked": "Control for the long-horizon suite: twelve sessions of chatter that is structurally identical to the other cases but teaches nothing the probe needs. Differences between this and the learning cases attribute to memory carrying; equality between this and an off-memory baseline of the same scaffold attributes to the harness or the model, not to learning.", "files": {"math.mjs": "export const sum = (xs) => xs.reduce((a, b) => a - b, 0);\n", ".freecode/settings.json": "{\"memory\":{\"autoConsolidate\":true,\"consolidateMinSessions\":1,\"consolidateMinHours\":0}}\n"}, "immutable": [".freecode/settings.json"], "sessions": ["Unrelated, but I work in IST (UTC+5:30), so if you ever mention times, use that zone. Don't change anything.", "Quickly: what does logging.mjs export? Just tell me, don't change anything.", "Reminder: I prefer vim over emacs. Just acknowledge, no edits.", "Where is the build pipeline configured? Just list, don't edit.", "Is there a queue module here? Just answer, don't edit.", "Quickly: does this repo have a returns module? Just answer, don't edit.", "I take coffee black, no sugar. Just acknowledge.", "What does metrics.mjs export? Just answer, don't change anything.", "Quickly: is there a shipping module? Just answer, don't edit.", "I prefer tabs over spaces in my personal projects. Don't change anything in this repo.", "What does cache.mjs export? Just answer, don't change anything.", "I prefer 4-space indentation for Python. Don't change anything."], "sessionFollowUps": [["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, no edits."], ["Just acknowledge, no edits."]], "consolidateBeforeFinal": true, "verify": "node --input-type=module -e \"import {sum} from './math.mjs'; import assert from 'node:assert'; assert.equal(sum([1,2,3]), 6); assert.equal(sum([]), 0); console.log('ok');\"", "expectMaxTurns": 15}
